//
// HUD text overlay: a small title line above a value line, at an exact pixel position.
// It is not a menu and never touches the menu stack. The script creates the widgets once,
// straight on the workspace, updates the value text, hides the overlay while any menu is
// open and unlinks it when the mission finishes.
//
// How the layout is built (rules measured on a live client, see references/gui-layouts.md):
//  - All four exact flags are 1, so position and size are layout units: 1 unit is 1 px at
//    1080 rows and H / 1080 px on a taller screen. Move or resize the root only; the two
//    text rows are laid out inside it.
//  - Every widget has ignorepointer 1, so the overlay never takes a click and nothing can
//    focus it. A FrameWidget without ignorepointer takes the mouse.
//  - priority counts among siblings only. The overlay is priority 1, so menu roots (2 and up) draw over it.
//  - Text uses an SDF font, which scales crisply. Its box must be tall enough or the text is
//    clipped: 13 pt needs about 19 units, 18 pt about 26. The Metron fonts have no U+0406
//    (Ukrainian capital I); see the Ukrainian letters section of references/gui-layouts.md.
//
// Script companion (client side, for example 5_Mission/MyMod/MyModHud.c). The load path
// starts at the mod's own pbo prefix:
//
